[cleanup] Retire superseded files, records, and filesystem residue (planning)
Files: proposals/redundancy-register.md; *.vine; proposals/**; crates/**; README.md; index.md; Cargo.toml; Cargo.lock; .github/**
Do: Apply the accepted collapse map. Delete empty/untracked residue, obsolete manifests, dead compatibility wrappers, superseded proposal copies, duplicate task nodes, stale links, and unused workspace members. Preserve user-authored changes, historical artifacts required by evidence, and any compatibility surface with a named consumer.
Accept: The repository contains no empty `caravan-windows` residue or equivalent unowned target directory; no deleted artifact is still referenced; Cargo, VINE, Markdown, and evidence maps are consistent; and cleanup diff is limited to register-approved redundancy.
-> code-collapse
-> evidence-collapse
-> plan-collapse
-> prose-collapse
> Files are deleted only when untracked/unowned or explicitly superseded by the register; historical proof is archived by reference rather than silently erased.
> Cleanup cannot alter authoritative engine behavior or sample meaning; it removes competing descriptions/implementations around them.
---
[review] Verify low-entropy architecture and close the redundancy pass (planning)
Files: redundancy.vine; proposals/redundancy-register.md; *.vine; proposals/**; crates/**; tests/**; evidence/**; .github/**
Do: Review the post-cleanup repository as an external consumer: locate the canonical contract, canonical plan, canonical implementation, canonical sample integration example, and primary evidence for each boundary. Run graph validation, dependency guards, formatting/lint, workspace/conformance, target-host compile, and designated runtime evidence.
Accept: An external reader can answer where each contract lives without searching competing records; no active duplicate owner remains; target-factory remediation has one downstream path; library/host/sample/target dependency direction passes guards; all VINE files validate; and the full declared evidence set is green.
-> cleanup
-> dependency-closure
-> evidence-collapse
> Closure is a measured reduction in competing owners and paths, not merely fewer files or fewer words.
> Any intentional remaining duplication is named as compatibility, historical evidence, generated output, or distinct consumer scope in the register.
